## Findings

**Symptom.** The user-facing slowdown is on `POST /api/v1/adminuserservice/users` through ts-ui-dashboard. Its p95 rose from about 92 ms to about 752 ms, while other dashboard endpoints stayed roughly flat. The 403 responses and route "not found" logs appear in both periods, so they are baseline noise.

**Root cause.** ts-auth-service's `AuthController.createDefaultUser` self-time grew sharply. Its mean went from 76 to 101 ms, and its p95 from 78 to 265 ms. The span's database children (`UserRepository.save`, `Transaction.commit`, the inserts) stayed at normal speed, so the extra time sits inside the method's own code. That makes it `application_method_slow`, not a database fault.

**Propagation.** The register chain runs ts-auth-service → ts-user-service → ts-admin-user-service → ts-ui-dashboard → user. Both ts-user-service's client POST to auth and its register server span show the wait, with the auth-side tail reaching roughly 0.7 s.

**Ruled out.** The other shifts in the survey are mostly traffic-mix changes or baseline noise. travelPlan/minStation p95 is 80 ms versus 112 ms normal. The route-service and user-service internal shifts are small (single-digit to low-teens ms) and don't connect to the user-facing path, so I did not name them.

